# device-overlay: hide the internal UFS from udisks, and so from Steam's Storage page
#
# What: marks every block device under the SoC's UFS host controller — the internal
#   storage: Android's partitions plus, since the internal install, Armada's own —
#   with UDISKS_IGNORE, which udisks2 exposes as HintIgnore=true on each object so
#   GUIs (Steam's Storage page, Dolphin) hide it. The objects still exist; nothing
#   that mounts the internal disk uses udisks (root/boot/ESP come from fstab and
#   ostree, the installer uses parted/lsblk), and the SD card sits on the mmc host,
#   so the steamos-automount path is untouched.
# Why: Android's partitions carry no filesystem Steam knows, so Steam listed the raw
#   chip as an empty drive ("MT512GAYAZ4U31, 464.5 GB free of 464.5 GB") next to the
#   SD card, inviting a Format that Armada's format-device.sh would refuse anyway
#   (2026-09-06, ledger L-12).
# Match: the parent chain (SUBSYSTEMS/KERNELS), not a drive letter — sd* names are
#   not stable, and the UFS host is "<addr>.ufs" on every Qualcomm handheld Armada
#   supports (1d84000.ufs on this SM8750), which is what makes this upstreamable.
# Block: B8 follow-up (cosmetic). First overlay file (v1).
# Apply without a reboot (a bare `udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=block` returned 1
#   and skipped these devices on 2026-09-06; the sysname match worked):
#   udevadm control --reload-rules && udevadm trigger -c change --subsystem-match=block --sysname-match='sd*'
# Revert: delete this file, then run the same two commands.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", SUBSYSTEMS=="platform", KERNELS=="*.ufs", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
